@section Title {
    <h1 id="Part1">De Testamento</h1>
    <h3>
        A Brief Exposition of the One and Eternal Testament or Covenant of God
    </h3>
}

@section DocumentContent {
    <h2>Introduction</h2>
    <br />
    <p>
        This brief discourse sets forth the one and eternal testament or
        covenant of God, which both the prophets, inspired with the
        divine spirit, and the apostles, commissioned by the Son of God,
        explained by writing entire books. As I begin, I especially pray
        for your spirit, Christ Jesus, in order that, imbued with it, I may
        be able to discourse clearly, briefly, soberly, and according to
        the analogy of faith concerning a subject that is difficult but at
        the same time necessary and useful.
    </p>
    <br />
    
    <p>
        First, however, in order that greater clarity and more certainty 
        may enter into the entire discussion it seems that a specific,
        definite meaning ought to be established for the word "testament," 
        because its usage varies in Scripture.
    </p>
    
